<title>GERMANY: TABLE - Karstadt - profits in line with goal. [CORRECTED 10:12 GMT]</title>
<headline>TABLE - Karstadt - profits in line with goal. [CORRECTED 10:12 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30:</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Parent sales				 5,545   up    0.3 pct</p>
<p>Sales by units</p>
<p>     Neckarmann Versand			1,463   down  1.9 pct</p>
<p>     Travel and tourism			  419   up    3.8 pct</p>
<p>     Hertie					1,721   down 12.6 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German retailer is Karstadt AG. The company said parent same store sales were down 3.3 percent.</p>
<p>Hertie same store sales were down 5.3 percent. Neckarmann Versand AG sales were 1.463 billion marks, a fall of 1.9 percent.</p>
<p>Walter Deuss, chief executive, said: &quot;Earnings developments in the Karstadt group to the end of May ... are in line with our planning. It is based on a group net profit of around 150 million marks (for 1997). This compares to 58.6 million marks in 1996.</p>
<p>(Corrects type of profit from &quot;group profit (on ordinary activities)&quot; and comparison figure from 117.7 million marks).</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097 150</p>
